nodes.goal:
INDEPENDENT read-back of the submission. The submit/draft records, when they ran, are auto-injected in ## Inputs as your direct parents; on a halt arm they are simply absent - then report arm=that halt from the echo record and touch nothing.
Otherwise take the PR url/number from the submit record and VERIFY IT FROM THE API, not from the submitter's prose: gh pr view --repo {run.base_repo} <number> --json number,state,headRefOid,baseRefName,title,body,url. Checks: state OPEN; headRefOid == preflight.head_sha (byte-equal); baseRefName == {run.base_branch}; title == draft.title; body carries the draft's ## Testing section. Any mismatch = verdict mismatch (name the field). Also record CI state if gh reports checks (pending/passing/failing - never act on it).
Reply with ONLY fenced json {"verdict": "verified|mismatch|none", "pr": "<url or empty>", "checks": {"state": "<OPEN|...>", "head_matches": true|false, "base_ok": true|false, "title_ok": true|false, "body_ok": true|false}, "ci": "<state or n/a>", "mismatch_fields": ["<field: expected vs observed>"], "arm": "submitted|preflight-halt|validate-halt|held"}
